{
  "id": "logging-logging",
  "slug": "logging",
  "title": "Logging",
  "category": "Spring Framework",
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "what-is-logging",
      "heading": "What is Logging?",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Logging is the process of recording log messages during the execution of a program to a centralized location (e.g., file, console, database). These logs track the steps, events, and exceptions within an application."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Purpose of Logging:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Diagnose and debug issues in the application.",
            "Maintain a historical record of system activity.",
            "Monitor and audit the application behavior.",
            "Improve maintainability by helping in post-error analysis."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 63,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "benefits-of-a-logging-framework",
          "heading": "Benefits of a Logging Framework",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Logging frameworks simplify and standardize how logging is performed. They offer:"
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": true,
              "items": [
                "Logging Levels: Categorize logs by severity (e.g., INFO, WARN, ERROR).",
                "Configurable Output Destination: Log messages can be stored in: ",
                "Pattern Formatting: Define how log messages appear.",
                "Performance Optimization: Efficient log writing, filtering, and management."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 45,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "popular-java-logging-frameworks",
          "heading": "Popular Java Logging Frameworks",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Framework",
                "Description"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "JDK Logging API",
                  "Built into Java (java.util.logging)"
                ],
                [
                  "Apache Log4j",
                  "Feature-rich and widely used"
                ],
                [
                  "Commons Logging API",
                  "Abstraction layer over other logging APIs"
                ],
                [
                  "Logback",
                  "Successor to Log4j; default in Spring Boot"
                ]
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 32,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "logging-in-spring-boot",
      "heading": "Logging in Spring Boot",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [],
      "wordCount": 0,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "default-behavior",
          "heading": "Default Behavior",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Spring Boot uses Apache Commons Logging as a facade.",
                "By default, Logback is used as the logging implementation."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 18,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "example",
          "heading": "Example:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "When running a Spring Boot application, you may see logs like:"
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "/Users/luffy/Desktop/Computer Science/Infosys/Spring Essentials/Logging/Logging/image.png",
              "alt": "image.png",
              "originalPath": "Logging/image.png"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "You didn’t write this code — it’s automatically logged by Spring Boot."
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 23,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "logging-levels-severity-hierarchy",
      "heading": "Logging Levels (Severity Hierarchy)",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Level",
            "Description"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "ALL",
              "Captures all log levels"
            ],
            [
              "TRACE",
              "Fine-grained informational events (useful for debugging)"
            ],
            [
              "DEBUG",
              "Debugging information"
            ],
            [
              "INFO",
              "General information about application progress"
            ],
            [
              "WARN",
              "Potentially harmful situations"
            ],
            [
              "ERROR",
              "Error events allowing the application to continue"
            ],
            [
              "FATAL",
              "Very severe errors; may lead to termination"
            ],
            [
              "OFF",
              "Disables all logging"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 47,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "example-use",
          "heading": "Example Use:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "INFO: A user logs into the app.",
                "ERROR: A database connection fails."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 12,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "configuring-logging-in-spring-boot",
      "heading": "Configuring Logging in Spring Boot",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Logging configurations are typically done in the application.properties file located at:"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "",
          "code": "src/main/resources/application.properties",
          "runnable": false
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 11,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "set-logging-levels",
          "heading": "Set Logging Levels",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "",
              "code": "logging.level.com.infy=INFO",
              "runnable": false
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Sets log level to INFO for all classes under com.infy."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 10,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "customize-console-log-pattern",
          "heading": "Customize Console Log Pattern",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "",
              "code": "logging.pattern.console=%d{yyyy-MMM-dd HH:mm:ss a} [%t] %-5level %logger{36} - %msg%n",
              "runnable": false
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Output:"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "",
              "code": "2025-May-02 10:45:12 AM [main] ERROR c.i.service.CusomerLoginServiceImpl - Service.WRONG_CREDENTIALS",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 1,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "customize-file-log-pattern",
          "heading": "Customize File Log Pattern",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "",
              "code": "logging.pattern.file=%d{yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss} [%thread] %-5level %logger{36} - %msg%n",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 0,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "log-to-file",
          "heading": "Log to File",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Name:"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "",
              "code": "logging.file.name=Error.log",
              "runnable": false
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "File path:"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "",
              "code": "logging.file.path=logs/Error.log",
              "runnable": false
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "📝 By default, Spring Boot logs only to the console."
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 13,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "using-log4j2-in-spring-boot",
      "heading": "Using Log4j2 in Spring Boot",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [],
      "wordCount": 0,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "1-exclude-default-logging",
          "heading": "1. Exclude Default Logging:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "In pom.xml:"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "xml",
              "code": "<dependency>\n    <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n    <artifactId>spring-boot-starter</artifactId>\n    <exclusions>\n        <exclusion>\n            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-logging</artifactId>\n        </exclusion>\n    </exclusions>\n</dependency>",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 2,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "2-add-log4j2-dependency",
          "heading": "2. Add Log4j2 Dependency:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "xml",
              "code": "<dependency>\n    <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n    <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-log4j2</artifactId>\n</dependency>",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 0,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "3-add-configuration-file",
          "heading": "3. Add Configuration File:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Place log4j2.properties (or .xml, .yaml) in the root of classpath."
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 10,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "4-using-log4j2-in-code",
          "heading": "4. Using Log4j2 in Code:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "java",
              "code": "import org.apache.logging.log4j.LogManager;\nimport org.apache.logging.log4j.Logger;\n\npublic class MyApp {\n    private static final Logger logger = LogManager.getLogger(MyApp.class);\n\n    public void doSomething() {\n        logger.info(\"App started\");\n        logger.error(\"Something went wrong!\");\n    }\n}",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 0,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "summary",
      "heading": "Summary",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Logging is essential for diagnostics and monitoring.",
            "Spring Boot uses Logback by default and can be customized extensively.",
            "Logging levels help prioritize issues.",
            "Output format and destination can be customized via application.properties.",
            "You can switch to other logging systems like Log4j2 by modifying dependencies and configurations."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 46,
      "subsections": []
    }
